        "id": 214691,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-23T09:35:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dprcooke\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dprcooke/48/1961_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dprcooke:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One thing I am curious about is what Parse was thinking when she shot the vat… Like, how is giving someone horrible chemical burns and sending them to crazy town preferable to killing them? Was she going for the irony and making MI fall to her own plot? Or did she see that this as somehow better? How \"far\" did she see the results of her action in this case?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I wonder if Parse's intent was to basically send Miss Info's consciousness back out into the ether like Miss Info was going to do to the F5 with said chemicals, only unfortunately it didn't actually work due to how wack Miss Info currently was.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:45:57.391Z",
